<article class="env-lemma" id="0G9Q">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0G9Q">Lemma <span data-tag="0G9Q">36.4.4</span>.</a> Let $X$ be a quasi-separated and quasi-compact scheme. For any object $K$ of $D_\mathit{QCoh}(\mathcal{O}_ X)$ the spectral sequence </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  E_2^{i, j} = H^ i(X, H^ j(K)) \Rightarrow H^{i + j}(X, K)  \]
</div>
  <p> of Cohomology, Example <a href="/tag/0BKM" data-tag="0BKM">20.29.3</a> is bounded and converges. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      By the construction of the spectral sequence via Cohomology, Lemma <a href="/tag/0BKK" data-tag="0BKK">20.29.1</a> using the filtration given by $\tau _{\leq -p}K$, we see that suffices to show that given $n \in \mathbf{Z}$ we have 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  H^ n(X, \tau _{\leq -p}K) = 0 \text{ for } p \gg 0  \]
</div>
    <p>
       and 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  H^ n(X, K) = H^ n(X, \tau _{\leq -p}K) \text{ for } p \ll 0  \]
</div>
    <p>
       The first follows from Lemma <a href="/tag/08D4" data-tag="08D4">36.3.4</a> applied with $F = \Gamma (X, -)$ and the bound in Cohomology of Schemes, Lemma <a href="/tag/01XJ" data-tag="01XJ">30.4.5</a>. The second holds whenever $-p \leq n$ for any ringed space $(X, \mathcal{O}_ X)$ and any $K \in D(\mathcal{O}_ X)$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>